{"id": "viva_meta_modelers_guide.composites.fig09a-coarse-graining", "name": "fig09a-coarse-graining", "description": "Fig 9a \u2014 self-organized processes, coarse-graining, and autopoiesis. Three functional COLUMNS \u2014 metabolism, containment, replication \u2014 each described at several GRAINS. In each column a coarse-grained CLOSURE process (sustains metabolites far from equilibrium; maintains a boundary; maintains/copies template information) is exactly what you get when the finer self-organized process (autocatalysis; membrane self-assembly; template replication) \u2014 and, below that, the molecular process (lipid aggregation; template-directed synthesis) \u2014 are lumped. Climbing each column is one rung of the coarse-graining ladder. The three columns are laid out side by side because their MUTUAL CLOSURE \u2014 metabolism supplying the energy and precursors that build the boundary and copy the template, containment holding the compartment that concentrates metabolism and replication, replication reproducing the machinery both need \u2014 is autopoiesis: the processes collectively produce and sustain the organization that enables them. All DRAFT processes: unit-bearing ports + behavior contracts, no update dynamics. Ports are wired to labeled stores so each quantity (and its unit) appears as a node.", "parameters": {}, "state": {"metabolism_closure": {"_type": "process", "address": "local:MetabolismClosure", "config": {"interval": 1.0}, "inputs": {"nutrients": ["metabolism_coarse", "nutrients"], "energy": ["metabolism_coarse", "energy"]}, "outputs": {"metabolites": ["metabolism_coarse", "metabolites"], "entropy": ["metabolism_coarse", "entropy"]}}, "metabolism_coarse": {"nutrients": {"_type": "chemical_flux", "_value": 0.0}, "energy": {"_type": "energy", "_value": 0.0}, "metabolites": {"_type": "concentration", "_value": 0.0}, "entropy": {"_type": "entropy", "_value": 0.0}}, "autocatalysis": {"_type": "process", "address": "local:Autocatalysis", "confi